          "reference": "A payments-table schema migration is squarely in the Opus-escalation set (auth/payments/migrations) — route the implementation to OPUS, not Sonnet and certainly not Haiku. Because it mutates payment data it is quality-sensitive: pair it with a VALIDATOR (builder-validator) and/or a backup + review before applying. Routing this to Haiku is the under-power trap the forbid anchor catches.",
